WEBVTT

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.620
Wh-What?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.840
Wind!

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.870
You really shouldn't underestimate heroes.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.630
Not that you did anything...

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.490
Thanks, Iu-chan.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.140
I'll lose some experience,

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.940
but I didn't have a choice.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.540
I do wish I know what that voice was...

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.410
But for now, we need to save 
Yotsuya-kun and Glen-san.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.330
Was that a monster I just heard?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.400
Probably. And a big one, too.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.270
Don't even try to run away.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.090
What was that noise earlier?

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.210
Sounded like a monster roaring.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.570
We should report to the village chief.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.330
O-Ow...

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.350
Are you all right, Froc?

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.980
This is nothing.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.870
But... I have to save Jezby.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.450
Save her?

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.530
But if you're chased out of 
the village like Dan was...

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.300
If that happens, I'll leave the village.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.160
Remember what Jezby said?

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.460
My brother went looking for 
a place called New Eden.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.200
Froc, you...

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.450
When I go, I'll take you, 
Jezby, and Lanan with me.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.240
Is that the house?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.420
Y-Yes.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.670
But look there.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.830
Looks like a bunch of people 
are flocking to it.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.410
What's going on?

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.880
You heard that monster's roar!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.510
We've never heard a roar that loud.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.870
Give us the village chief!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.090
Chief Cox is away from home at the moment.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.360
Hey, look!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.260
The chief!

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.610
And aren't those heroes walking with him?

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.840
In this village?

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.490
Wait, why is the village chief 
being held captive by heroes?

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.690
A-All I did was carry out my 
duty as the village chief

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.350
by capturing Jezby, who broke our rules!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.590
Jezby?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.750
Chief Cox?

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.600
Oh, right! That little girl!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.930
Bayne's little girl, Jezby!

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.530
The girl who fled the village alone!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.170
These people showed up here with Jezby!

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.460
And when I attempted to capture 
her, they did this to me!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.420
Why would heroes do such a thing?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.620
They were obviously sent here by 
outsiders to take Zagroth from us!

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.260
Huh?

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.130
It's impressive how he just spews 
out one lie after another.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.500
Let Jezby go!

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.170
Froc?

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.560
You said you'd forgive Jezby! You lied!

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.000
Of course I did.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.980
I cannot allow anyone to break the rules 
of this village, not even a child!

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.370
Grab him!

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.910
Stay away! What are you gonna do?!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.210
Quiet down!

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.610
Why, you...

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.030
Little punk!

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.530
Settle down!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.120
Stop!

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.580
Outta my way!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.000
I said settle down!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.660
Um...

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.480
Wait!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.780
I don't care why you people 
came to this village,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.800
Just leave quietly.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.390
Froc!

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.590
Mom!

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.750
How could you do this to a child?

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.860
Aren't you a father yourself?

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.430
Have you no shame?!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.230
It's no use.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.470
Froc?!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.470
Anyone who defies the chief 
or does anything out of line

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:11.840
will be sent on the Journey of Hope, 
like my brother and Bayne.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.070
We all have no choice but to curry 
favor with each other to survive.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.020
What does a mere child know?

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.590
The reason Zagroth enjoys peace is—

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.220
This mother and child sheltered Jezby!

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.190
They bring disaster to the 
village, just like Jezby!

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.640
That monster's roar proves it!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.810
Disaster?

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.050
But that can't be...

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:45.820
If they aren't captured, disaster 
will befall this village!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:46.910
H-Hey!

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.350
You two, come with us!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.320
You little...

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.050
It's no use resisting!

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:53.820
Stop!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.750
Keep your hands off my mom!

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.520
Those who disturb the village's 
peace shall not be—

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.810
Huh?!

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:10.290
I'm gonna make all of you bastards pay!

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.360
Uh...

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.080
Violence toward humans, 
like hitting or kicking them, is...

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:17.980
Oh, boy.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.420
Help!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.910
The hero's gonna kill us!

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.600
Run!

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.240
I said stop, damn it!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:32.300
If you don't set Yuusuke and Glen-san 
free right now, I'll kill you.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.000
Don't you dare underestimate heroes!

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.790
m 0 0 l 200 0 l 200 170 l 0 170

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.790
<b>Torii Keita
Warrior (Spear)  Rank 5→3

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.590
And that just wiped out all the experience 
he gained in the limestone cave.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.590
Who's this girl?

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.550
Iris...

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.800
How dare you hit my grandpa?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.930
He's the most important person here!

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.070
His granddaughter?

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.980
I tossed the key to the 
dungeon down the old well.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.960
What?!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.760
Where is this well?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.270
Behind my house.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:15.250
But the bottom of the well gave out 
years ago, and it's all dried up.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.610
You'll never get the key back.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:18.660
Oh, no...

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.240
You got what you deserved.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.030
This little brat...

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.430
Jezby, are you okay?

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:26.860
Yeah. Thanks, Froc.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.460
Nah, I didn't do anything.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.560
No, I'm just happy you 
came to try to save me.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.310
M-Mom, where's Lanan?

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:40.240
Oh, gosh! I ran out in such a hurry...

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.070
Jezby, go back with my mom.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.640
What about you?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.580
I'm going to see the heroes.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.360
The village chief might still 
be plotting something.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.180
Don't be too reckless.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:53.880
I won't.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:58.620
Again?

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.690
Whoa! An earthquake?!

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:06.810
Huh?

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.970
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 170 l 0 170

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.970
<b>[Monsters]</b>

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.970
Creatures that attack any humans or players they
detect. This behavior takes priority over all other
actions for them. The more magical power they
have, the stronger and more aggressive they are.
There are many regular animal species (such as
horses) that are considered separate from
monsters.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:18.460
There's trouble!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.320
A monster!

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.380
We've never seen a monster 
that big before...

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.850
That's not all.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:36.370
There are a bunch of them.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.820
This is a lot more than we 
can even hope to fight.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.250
Why?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.660
This is the end of my village...

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:47.450
Can't you just have those guys kill them?

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:48.880
They're heroes, aren't they?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.070
Look, shorty...

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.460
I'm not "shorty"! I'm Iris!

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.750
I'll call you whatever the hell I want!

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:58.100
You're the one who threw away the key!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.520
The key is...

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.250
What?!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.600
The monsters are already...

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.510
"Already" what?

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.060
Huh?

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.710
Glen-san?

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.690
Yotsuya-kun!

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.330
Huh? Guys?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:34.180
Chief, what's up with that dungeon?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.850
Since it's underground, 
the walls are solid.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.990
And do these iron bars mean it's 
supposed to be a dungeon?

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.940
But what's the point when 
the ceiling is just wood?

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.650
I can hear sound coming from above.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:51.560
Based on our location, 
we're right below the reception hall.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:52.800
Yeah.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.690
So anyway, we made it out.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.050
All these monsters are stronger 
than they should be.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.250
The situation is pretty dire.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.830
Putting that giant one aside,

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.660
how did they climb up the cliffs outside?

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.430
Did they ride on that one's back?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.670
But they're not the same species. 
Does that even happen?

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.020
What should we do?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:26.590
It looks like it'll take them less than 
ten minutes to make it to the village.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:31.230
<i>Did "destruction" refer to the 
area this village is in?</i>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.060
<b>Stop the destruction of the village of Zagroth.</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.060
<b>(Time limit: 30 days)</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.060
<b>Quest Time!</b>

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.910
<i>Or did it refer to the people living here?</i>

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:39.040
<i>But in these circumstances, 
there's only one choice.</i>

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:44.080
It's impossible for us to take out that 
swarm of monsters as we are now.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.150
Let's escape by the tunnel 
we came in through.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:51.640
No, the monsters are dropping down from 
right above the entrance to that tunnel.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:54.530
If we go there now, 
we'll run right into them.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.550
I'll go tell the villagers!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.770
Froc-kun!

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.770
I'll bring them here.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.900
I'm sure the heroes here will 
do something about it!

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:07.180
Huh?

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.990
What do we do?

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.880
What choice do we have but to fight?

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:15.070
Are you nuts? You could barely 
survive a fight with a bat!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.870
Shut up, glasses!

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.700
Glasses are a recognized attribute!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.750
Huh? Attri— 
The hell are you talking about?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.840
They won't come loose!

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.540
There might be an escape route...

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:35.040
You said the bottom fell out of 
this well and it dried up, right?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.630
Y-Yes. There was an earthquake, 
and the water dried up.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:43.420
I ordered an investigation, but it was 
too deep, so we just sealed it up.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.130
If the bottom fell out, it might 
lead to that limestone cave.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.860
That's definitely possible, but...

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:54.070
Even if we can escape underground 
through this well...

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:56.150
I'll go down first to test it.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.180
How are you going to get down?

00:11:58.470 --> 00:11:59.780
I'll jump down.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:03.490
As a Heavy Warrior, I have 
the strongest armor.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.320
Huh?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:04.900
Wait...

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:09.330
I might die, but you guys will 
be able to find my location.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:12.040
But there might be muddy 
water running below.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.750
And not just that. 
We don't know what's down there.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.750
If it doesn't work, we'll 
just leave it alone.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:20.010
I think it's worth trying,

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.110
even if we have to sacrifice one pawn.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.670
Right, Yotsuya-kun?

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:27.040
Huh? Uh... Y-Yeah, I guess.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.150
<i>She's not wrong, but why'd 
she say that to me?</i>

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.480
I'm just going to do what I can.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.020
Yes!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>Reviving</b>

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>Hakozaki Kusue</b>

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.650
She's moving again!

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:46.290
Looks like there's ground to stand on.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:55.280
One, two, three.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:56.660
This is...

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.720
...really dangerous, isn't it?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.460
The little ones are already 
reaching the village.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.310
How much more should we cut?

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:11.660
Hakozaki-san counted to three 
before she hit the bottom,

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:15.340
so if we assume it's 40 meters, 
we just need enough for that much.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.490
Help me tie these up, please.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:18.360
Sure.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:18.360
Okay.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:22.020
Cheer up, Grandpa.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.250
The heroes said they're gonna save us.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.380
If the village of Zagroth 
is lost, I'll be...

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:28.990
I'm sorry, Iris.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.190
<i>So they closed off the village to minimize 
the risk of it being destroyed,</i>

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:37.000
<i>and he ruled over that 
tiny, closed-off world?</i>

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.520
<i>What scum.</i>

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.800
Don't worry.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.800
Even if the village is lost, my grandpa 
is the most important person here.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.900
<i>He'll have no more authority.</i>

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.250
Help!

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.220
Here they come! Hurry!

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:53.420
That's all?

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:16.880
Are you serious?

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:18.880
What about Jezby's group?!

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:25.060
Jezby... Mom... Lanan...

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.520
Froc!

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.120
Jezby! Lanan!

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:37.100
Look out!

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.130
Lanan, Jezby...

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.200
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:44.680
Where's my mom?

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:49.250
When we were running away... 
She was protecting us...

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.290
Damn it...

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.750
Let's run to the chief's house!

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:08.610
You can do it!

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.840
Just take them one at a time, 
and you'll be fine!

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.720
Careful, Jezby.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:21.610
Okay.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:27.550
What now?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.120
They're looking this way...

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:29.940
Yeah...

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.870
You okay, Froc?

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.970
Yeah. Lanan, come down one at a time.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:36.310
Go ahead.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:40.770
Shindou-san and Glen-san, 
you two go down first.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.200
I'll go get the two guards.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.970
Iris!

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:53.980
It's okay.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:56.420
You're okay now.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.110
Thank you...

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.130
Iris! Are you hurt? 
You're not hurt, are you?!

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.490
No.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.260
F-Forgive me, Great Hero.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.640
What I did to you...

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:19.670
More are still coming down, right? 
Please help them.

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.420
R-Right...

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.960
Get to the well, you two!

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:26.420
Hurry!

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:30.670
They all started heading this 
way at once! We're in trouble!

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:33.650
The ladder!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.250
They're...

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.770
No other choice now. We have to...

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.600
...die, huh?

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.210
Whoa, watch it! Don't pull 
that! I'm gonna fall!

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.690
Once the time came to do it, I got scared!

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:02.530
<i>These guys didn't just wander in here.</i>

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.370
<i>They're clearly trying 
to destroy the village.</i>

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.130
<i>They're not like the orcs on Jiffon Island.</i>

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:16.200
<i>It's almost like someone's 
controlling them...</i>

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.270
I'm back!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.490
They all really did come back to life!

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:32.060
Heroes are amazing!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.700
I thought I was gonna die.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.930
Yeah, you <i>did</i> die.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.910
We can't stay long. 
We should keep moving.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:40.790
You're right.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:47.710
We made it out.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.260
It took about six hours after 
we came down the well.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.700
I guess we should consider ourselves lucky.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:55.330
We got out, but if we just keep this up...

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:56.840
Yeah...

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:00.030
So now we take all our 
stuff and... do what?

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.480
They're not "stuff."

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.630
These people are important 
for completing the quest.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.720
Even if the monsters destroy the village,

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.210
the fact that we're still here 
can mean only one thing.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:12.710
What does that mean?

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:13.820
You don't get it?

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:19.790
If they were all dead, 
it'd be game over for us.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:26.850
Are you okay, Jezby?

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.910
Yeah. How about you, Lanan?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.500
I'm tired! I can't walk anymore!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:37.430
Iris, if we stay here,

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:40.980
there's no telling when the 
monsters will come after us.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:45.190
But my feet hurt, and I'm hungry!

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:49.090
If you don't want to die, perhaps you 
wouldn't mind walking, please?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.270
No!

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:52.130
<i>This little...</i>

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.360
Want me to carry you on my back, then?

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.280
Really?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.330
Torii the Hero is great at piggyback rides.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.290
Yay!

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.220
A piggyback ride from a hero!

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:04.700
Man, you're so light, Iris.

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:08.750
<i>You were just calling her "stuff" earlier.</i>

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.060
He switches gears so quickly.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:16.800
It looks like we came out on the opposite 
side from where we entered the village.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.600
I guess maps don't do any good, then.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:23.110
What is it?

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.040
That's...

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.720
not a game trail.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:31.350
It looks like it was formed by people 
walking back and forth a lot.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:36.770
But the person who led us here said there 
were no towns or anything on this side.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.120
Was it goblins?

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.350
If so, this area is dangerous, too.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.410
Why don't we check it out, Yuusuke?

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.030
Just walking around blindly 
certainly won't get us anywhere.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.260
So on that note, 
Glen-san and I will go investigate.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.990
Okay, I'll go, too.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.270
Wait here, okay?

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.180
No!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:59.380
Torii the Hero has to stay with me!

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.900
Nice to see that girls actually 
like you this time.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.100
Lay off!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.600
There's no guarantee the monster 
won't attack here, too.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.840
We'll just do a minimal investigation.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.510
Take care of the rest.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:17.240
There's actually a settlement here?

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.180
Is it a thieves' hideout?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:24.750
But attacking anywhere from a remote place 
like this wouldn't be very efficient.

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.190
It's hard to believe.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:28.590
Glen-san?

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.290
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.500
A proverb?! This auto-translation 
thing is amazing!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.120
Looks like no one's around.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.790
I guess we can use this place as a base.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:47.250
Even better if there's 
something we can eat...

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:49.630
Was that...

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:50.430
Yeah.

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:56.930
Huh? Bayne-san wasn't your real dad?

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:57.890
That's right.

00:20:57.890 --> 00:21:01.910
He took me in when I was 
orphaned as a small child.

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:05.240
That was ages ago. He might 
as well be your real dad.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:09.410
Yeah. If he wasn't, he wouldn't 
have left the village.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.410
Jezby...

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.950
My village is gone.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.420
What am I to do now?

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.960
What else? All you can do 
is try the best you can.

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:35.480
You've got Iris, after all, Grandpa.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.440
Yes... You're right.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.910
<b>The Monsters Attack</b>

